  <!-- ========== FAQ ========== -->
  <section class="section faq-section" id="faq" style="background: var(--bg-alt);" aria-label="Frequently asked questions about SEO in Singapore">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-header reveal">
        <p class="section-label">FAQ</p>
        <h2><span class="highlight">SEO &amp; Performance</span> — Questions <span class="highlight">Answered</span></h2>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-list">
        <details class="faq-item reveal reveal-d1">
          <summary>How long does SEO take to show results?</summary>
          <div class="faq-answer"><p>SEO is a long-term strategy. Most businesses start seeing noticeable improvements in organic traffic within 3–6 months. Competitive keywords may take longer, but quick wins like fixing technical issues can show results within weeks.</p></div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item reveal reveal-d2">
          <summary>Can you guarantee first page rankings?</summary>
          <div class="faq-answer"><p>No legitimate SEO agency can guarantee specific rankings — Google's algorithm considers hundreds of factors. What we guarantee is a data-driven approach, transparent reporting, and continuous optimisation to improve your search visibility over time.</p></div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item reveal reveal-d3">
          <summary>What's included in the monthly SEO report?</summary>
          <div class="faq-answer"><p>Our reports cover keyword rankings, organic traffic trends, top-performing pages, backlink profile, Core Web Vitals scores, and actionable recommendations. Reporting cadence and strategy-call frequency are scoped to your engagement on the discovery call.</p></div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item reveal reveal-d1">
          <summary>How is SEO different from paid ads?</summary>
          <div class="faq-answer"><p>SEO drives free organic traffic by improving your site's visibility in search results — results compound over time. Paid ads deliver immediate traffic but stop the moment you pause spending. Most businesses benefit from combining both strategies.</p></div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item reveal reveal-d2">
          <summary>Do I need a new website before starting SEO?</summary>
          <div class="faq-answer"><p>Not necessarily. We can optimise most existing websites. However, if your site has serious technical issues, slow performance, or an outdated design, we may recommend improvements first. Our technical audit will identify exactly what needs fixing.</p></div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item reveal reveal-d3">
          <summary>How much does an SEO agency cost in Singapore?</summary>
          <div class="faq-answer"><p>Pricing depends on your goals, your market, and the scope of work — there's no one-size package. Book a quick consultation and we'll scope exactly what you need and give you a transparent quote.</p></div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item reveal reveal-d1">
          <summary>How do I choose the best SEO agency in Singapore?</summary>
          <div class="faq-answer"><p>Look for four things: a clear, data-driven approach (not guaranteed-rankings promises — no legitimate agency can guarantee positions), transparent monthly reporting, real results you can verify, and whether they optimise for AI search (Google's AI Overview, ChatGPT, Gemini) rather than classic Google rankings alone. Ask for a free audit first so you can judge the thinking before you commit.</p></div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item reveal reveal-d2">
          <summary>Do you optimise for AI search and Google's AI Overview (GEO)?</summary>
          <div class="faq-answer"><p>Yes — it is a core part of our SEO. Beyond classic Google rankings, we optimise so your business is cited in AI answers across Google's AI Overview, ChatGPT, Gemini and Perplexity. We practise what we sell: Jraft Creative got its own site cited in Google's AI Overview, and we apply the same <a href="/geo-agency-singapore/">GEO approach</a> for clients — <a href="/blog/how-we-got-cited-in-google-ai-overview-singapore/">here's exactly how we did it</a>.</p></div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item reveal reveal-d3">
          <summary>What is SEO?</summary>
          <div class="faq-answer"><p>SEO — Search Engine Optimisation — is the practice of improving your website so it appears higher in unpaid Google results when people search for what you offer. It covers three areas: technical SEO (making the site fast and easy for Google to read), on-page SEO (making each page clearly relevant to a search), and off-page SEO (building the authority and links that earn trust). In 2026 it also means optimising to be cited in AI answers like Google's AI Overview.</p></div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item reveal reveal-d1">
          <summary>Why is SEO important for a Singapore business?</summary>
          <div class="faq-answer"><p>Because most buying decisions in Singapore start with a search, and most searchers never look past page one. SEO puts you in front of people at the exact moment they're looking to buy — and unlike ads, the traffic doesn't stop when you stop paying. For local businesses, it also captures the "near me" map-pack searches that drive walk-ins and calls.</p></div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item reveal reveal-d2">
          <summary>Is SEO a short-term or long-term strategy?</summary>
          <div class="faq-answer"><p>Long-term. Technical fixes can produce quick wins in weeks, but building rankings and authority for competitive terms takes months and compounds over time. That's the trade-off versus paid ads: SEO is slower to start but keeps working — and getting cheaper per lead — the longer you invest. Anyone promising overnight rankings is selling something that won't last.</p></div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item reveal reveal-d3">
          <summary>Should I invest in SEO or Google Ads?</summary>
          <div class="faq-answer"><p>Most businesses benefit from both. Google Ads buys immediate visibility while your SEO builds — useful at launch or for time-sensitive offers. SEO earns durable, compounding traffic that lowers your cost per lead over time. A common approach is ads for speed now, SEO for the long game, then shift the mix as your organic rankings climb. We'll advise the right split on the discovery call.</p></div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item reveal reveal-d1">
          <summary>Are backlinks still important in 2026?</summary>
          <div class="faq-answer"><p>Yes — quality backlinks are still one of Google's strongest trust signals, and they increasingly influence which brands AI engines cite too. What's changed is that quality and relevance matter far more than volume. A handful of links from reputable, on-topic Singapore sources beats hundreds of cheap directory links, which can actively harm you. We build authority the durable way, not the spammy way.</p></div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item reveal reveal-d2">
          <summary>What types of businesses do you do SEO for?</summary>
          <div class="faq-answer"><p>We run vertical-specific SEO across clinics and aesthetics, tuition and enrichment, preschools, F&amp;B and restaurants, beauty and hair salons, spas, gyms and fitness studios, music schools, interior designers, and more. The signals that rank a clinic differ from those that rank a tuition centre, so we use industry-specific playbooks rather than a one-size template.</p></div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item reveal reveal-d3">
          <summary>Do you do local SEO and Google Business Profile?</summary>
          <div class="faq-answer"><p>Yes. For any business with a physical location or a service area, local SEO is often the fastest win. We optimise your Google Business Profile, build consistent local citations, set up a review strategy, and target the map pack for "near me" and location-based searches — the highest-intent, closest-to-conversion traffic there is.</p></div>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

